cluster: retain one Ed25519 host key per KB guest

The node's volatile root regenerated host keys after resume. Store its
single Ed25519 key on the mounted retained tank and refuse unavailable or
unsafe storage before the existing OS key-generation loop can run.

Use the same explicit algorithm for services and optional DNS guests on
their retained writable roots. One advertised key avoids accepting a
partial initial multi-algorithm set that strict retained trust later refuses.

This policy requires genuinely new artifacts. It neither migrates older
volatile or multi-key guests nor enlarges their retained client trust.
